Replay scripts contain WORD packets, not DWORDs. Original Record_Event
0x4479b1/0x4479c5/0x4479f4/0x447a02 advances the cursor by TWO bytes and
0x447a07 stores AX. Control_Car_Replay 0x4476e9 advances by TWO and reads
WORDs at 0x4476fa/0x44771d/0x447737/0x447756. Terminate_Replay_Bodge
0x447a74/0x447a7f stores only one WORD, preserving the next packet.

Retype both script lvalues and cursor aliases; the end-pointer storage is a
32-bit pointer to WORD. int* cursor arithmetic previously skipped a packet
on every action change and Bodge cleared its neighbor. Native and WASM
isolated actual-engine fixtures reject both against literal original x86
functions. No replay bytes, engine state or input is substituted in gameplay.

